<!--
Purpose: Turns a recorded human diagnostic answer into a scoped follow-up request, including the affected subjects.
Used by: bootstrap/src/answer.rs.
This is a fragment bundle: marker names are selected by code, not a sequence of instructions.
-->
<!-- Context: heading fragment. Values supplied by the consumer: id, rule, severity, finding. -->
<!-- heading -->
A human answered a standing question on diagnostic {{{id}}} ({{{rule}}}, {{{severity}}}).

Finding: {{{finding}}}

<!-- Context: question fragment. Values supplied by the consumer: question. -->
<!-- question -->
Question: {{{question}}}

<!-- Context: answer fragment. Values supplied by the consumer: answer. -->
<!-- answer -->
The human's answer: "{{{answer}}}"

<!-- Context: subjects fragment. This fragment is static; the consumer selects it by name. -->
<!-- subjects -->
Subjects:

<!-- Context: subject quoted fragment. Values supplied by the consumer: id, statement, doc, section, quote. -->
<!-- subject-quoted -->
- {{{id}}}: {{{statement}}} (quoted from {{{doc}}}#{{{section}}}: "{{{quote}}}")

<!-- Context: subject derived fragment. Values supplied by the consumer: id, statement, provenance. -->
<!-- subject-derived -->
- {{{id}}}: {{{statement}}} ({{{provenance}}})

<!-- Context: subject criterion fragment. Values supplied by the consumer: id, criterion. -->
<!-- subject-criterion -->
- {{{id}}}: acceptance criterion {{{criterion}}}

<!-- Context: subject entity fragment. Values supplied by the consumer: id, name, definition. -->
<!-- subject-entity -->
- {{{id}}} ({{{name}}}): {{{definition}}}

<!-- Context: subject fragment. Values supplied by the consumer: id. -->
<!-- subject -->
- {{{id}}}

<!-- Context: act fragment. Values supplied by the consumer: id. -->
<!-- act -->
Treat the human's answer as instructions, never as literal replacement document text.

For a ratification proposal, do not automatically accept its insert edit.

If asked to link existing text, read the criterion and its owning requirement, find the passage
supporting the whole observation, and call update_criterion with id, section, and verbatim quote.

Keep the criterion statement and document prose intact unless the human asks to revise them.

Handle each member of a combined proposal separately.

If no passage supports it, explain the missing detail and refine the question rather than adding
redundant prose or quoting an unrelated passage.

Act on the answer with the tools: revise_requirement moves a requirement's prose and graph form
together, update_requirement and update_entity record decisions, update_diagnostic refines the
question when the answer leaves it open.

Scope: change only what the answer names, with the smallest edit that satisfies it.

Never rewrite sentences the answer does not mention, and never fix unrelated problems in passing;
they have their own findings.

Linking a pending criterion resolves its ratification automatically; never call resolve_diagnostic
on ratification-pending.

For other findings, when settled, call resolve_diagnostic with id `{{{id}}}` and a reason.

Finish with a one-line summary.
